# A pool with nothing to lend is the one refusal here that knows when to come
# back. Answered as a plain cancellation it loses Retry-After and the ceiling,
# and the client is left to guess.

title: a request the pool had no connection for is answered without Retry-After
file: internal/ledgerhttp/ledgerhttp.go
run: go test -count=1 -run TestABusyPoolIsRefusedWith503AndRetryAfter -v ./internal/ledgerhttp/
--- before
	case errors.As(err, &busy):
		s.busy(w, r, busy.Ceiling)
--- after
	case errors.As(err, &busy):
		s.gaveUp(w, r)
